Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.04,0:00:06.40,Flashback Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,It's been one week since the Grieving Souls \Nbegan operating in the capital of Zebrudia.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.10,0:00:10.41,Flashback,Luke,0,0,0,,I wasn't expecting this.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.79,0:00:12.76,Flashback,Luke,0,0,0,,I can't believe that my \Nultimate divine sword,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.76,0:00:15.32,Flashback,Luke,0,0,0,,the Testament Blade, \Nwould break just like that!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.91,0:00:18.19,Flashback,Liz,0,0,0,,I mean, it {\i1}was{\i0} a wooden sword...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.19,0:00:20.57,Flashback,Sitri,0,0,0,,That's pushing it when \Ngoing up against phantoms.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.57,0:00:25.54,Flashback,Lucia,0,0,0,,But I never expected to encounter a \Ncyclops in a level 1 treasure vault...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.54,0:00:27.36,Flashback,Liz,0,0,0,,It was {\i1}so{\i0} strong!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.36,0:00:28.05,Flashback,Lucia,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.05,0:00:31.14,Flashback,Sitri,0,0,0,,Cyclopes are at least a level 4.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.14,0:00:34.23,Flashback,Sitri,0,0,0,,At least, that's what it said \Nin the material I read.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.23,0:00:35.02,Flashback,Ansem,0,0,0,,Yup.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.27,0:00:38.42,Flashback,Yoidore,0,0,0,,A cyclops, you say?!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.75,0:00:42.11,Flashback,Yoidore,0,0,0,,What the hell are you talking \Nabout, damn rookies?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.11,0:00:45.50,Flashback,Yoidore,0,0,0,,As if something like {\i1}that{\i0} would \Never appear in the Goblin Cave!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.50,0:00:47.16,Flashback,Yoidore,0,0,0,,Oh, is that it?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.16,0:00:48.81,Flashback,Yoidore,0,0,0,,Since you're here,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.81,0:00:52.32,Flashback,Yoidore,0,0,0,,you actually managed to run \Naway from the cyclops?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.53,0:00:55.85,Flashback,Sitri,0,0,0,,Poke, poke.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.85,0:00:56.32,Flashback,Yoidore,0,0,0,,Hmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.00,0:00:59.34,Flashback,Yoidore,0,0,0,,What's that, girlie?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.61,0:01:01.06,Flashback,Liz,0,0,0,,Look, old-timer.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.45,0:01:08.10,Flashback,Yoidore,0,0,0,,It's an eyeball!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.96,0:01:12.60,Flashback Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,That's why I told you \Nto not take the head.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.74,0:01:18.21,Internal,Narrator,0,0,0,,We are now in the golden age \Nof the treasure hunters!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.21,0:01:21.37,Internal,Narrator,0,0,0,,Amid the sparkling talent on \Ndisplay in the capital of Zebrudia,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.37,0:01:24.27,Internal,Narrator,0,0,0,,there was one man who stood \Nout amongst all others!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.27,0:01:26.47,Internal,Narrator,0,0,0,,His name is Krai Andrey.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.47,0:01:29.07,Internal,Narrator,0,0,0,,This is an epic tale \Nfull of glory and agony,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.07,0:01:31.04,Internal,Narrator,0,0,0,,of how he became renowned \Nfor being the leader
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.04,0:01:33.94,Internal,Narrator,0,0,0,,of the strongest party he founded \Nwith his childhood friends,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.94,0:01:37.13,Internal,Narrator,0,0,0,,and also the master of the strongest clan!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.58,0:02:42.27,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,So how long will this head stay around?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.27,0:02:44.97,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,It will eventually turn into \Nmana material and disappear.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.97,0:02:46.20,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Since it's a phantom.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.47,0:02:49.48,EpTitle,Title,0,0,0,,{\c&H00BAFF&\pos(320.52,100.623)}Episode 03
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.47,0:02:49.48,EpTitle,Title,0,0,0,,{\fs30\bord3\pos(322.143,238.714)\c&HD1D1D1&}I Want to Fly Straight Through the Sky
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.48,0:02:48.71,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,"I Want to Fly Straight Through the Sky."
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.20,0:03:07.95,Show Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,700)\pos(324,269)\fscx95\fscy76}Let This Grieving Soul Retire
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.18,0:03:31.20,Default,Rhuda,0,0,0,,That didn't look like something that \Nwould appear in a level 3 treasure vault.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.30,0:03:36.60,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,Sheesh, that thing sure was tough!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.60,0:03:38.06,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,There was only one.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.19,0:03:41.20,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,We had the numerical advantage.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.20,0:03:44.45,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah. How come \Nyou didn't use your fire?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.45,0:03:47.07,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,Oh, well, about that...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.07,0:03:48.07,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.07,0:03:50.52,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,The Purgatorial Sword is out of mana.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.52,0:03:51.11,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.11,0:03:51.83,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.83,0:03:53.07,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,Because of back then!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.39,0:03:57.82,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,I can't charge it myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.09,0:04:01.48,Default,Rhuda,0,0,0,,Hey. Maybe it would be better \Nif we retreated for now...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.48,0:04:03.73,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,These conditions are completely \Ndifferent from what was outlined.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.73,0:04:05.15,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,I bet under these circumstances,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.15,0:04:07.49,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,the people we're supposed \Nto rescue are already dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.49,0:04:09.10,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,We're sticking to the plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.10,0:04:12.22,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Not to mention, we haven't \Neven entered the vault yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.22,0:04:13.49,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,Hold up.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.49,0:04:16.27,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,At the end of the day, surviving \Nis more important, right?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.27,0:04:18.72,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,If another one of those \N things comes at us again...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.72,0:04:21.89,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,It seems you are still \Nconfused, Great Greg.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.89,0:04:23.10,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,Just Greg is fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.10,0:04:25.59,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,It seems you are still confused, Greg.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.59,0:04:27.83,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,We're not here to collect the dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.83,0:04:30.00,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Those people {\i1}are{\i0} still alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.29,0:04:32.45,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,We're executing a level 8's\N inscrutable strategy.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.92,0:04:35.26,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Master's decision making is infallible.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.49,0:04:39.62,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,The Purgatorial Sword's mana being depleted \Nmust also be a part of Master's plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.46,0:04:42.01,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,You mean he did it on purpose?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.09,0:04:45.45,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,He's telling us not to rely on relics.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.23,0:04:55.27,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,Hey, some of them have bows and guns.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.27,0:04:59.15,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,So it's not like the one we\Nencountered was just an outlier.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.55,0:05:04.25,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,The White Wolf's Den was \Ncreated to suit the size
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.25,0:05:07.15,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,of the Silver Moon wolf monsters\N that originally lived here.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.43,0:05:11.29,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Being so large, they probably can't \Nmove that well inside the den.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.29,0:05:13.97,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,So you're saying that rather \Nthan fighting in the open,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.97,0:05:16.16,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,we should hurry and get inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.40,0:05:18.65,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,I'm going in.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.24,0:05:22.91,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,If we can get rid of the bows and guns, \Nthe rest should be manageable somehow.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.14,0:05:23.93,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Are you an idiot,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.93,0:05:24.59,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,or a dumbass,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.59,0:05:25.54,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,or a numpty?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.02,0:05:29.94,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,Even without mana, the Purgatorial Sword \Nis stronger than a regular sword!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.94,0:05:31.77,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Don't do anything rash.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.77,0:05:35.54,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,As the leader, it's my duty \Nto get you all back alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.54,0:05:36.20,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.20,0:05:40.95,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,This time, Master is counting on me \Nto act in the capacity of a leader.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.30,0:05:45.82,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Returning home with every single member \Nalive is essentially the bare minimum.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.37,0:05:49.52,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,As Rhuda and I are nimble, \Nwe'll draw the enemy to us first.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.52,0:05:53.75,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Then the two of you assault \Ntheir back line from behind.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.75,0:05:56.09,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Their ranged weapons won't \Nbe so scary if we get close.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.35,0:05:59.06,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Even if things turn dangerous,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.06,0:06:02.35,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,we won't use anyone as a \Nshield, or sacrifice them.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.13,0:06:08.58,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,Please, let at least Tino be alive!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.92,0:06:12.54,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,Even if she has to use the rest\Nof the party as meat shields!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.37,0:06:17.23,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,The enemy outweighs us \Nconsiderably in skill.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.02,0:06:22.36,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,But we do have one thing going for us.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.73,0:06:24.72,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,Teamwork.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.51,0:06:27.99,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,All right!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.99,0:06:29.34,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,Dammit.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.34,0:06:31.75,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,This really {\i1}is{\i0} an unreasonable job.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.02,0:06:36.25,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,As expected, it's not so difficult to \Ndefeat them with four people on our side.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.63,0:06:38.54,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,No matter how strong they are,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.54,0:06:41.78,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,the enemy has no concept of cooperation.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.58,0:06:48.89,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,Here they come.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.88,0:06:52.38,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,We'll cut them to ribbons!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.64,0:06:58.69,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,Even though it's an ad-hoc party, \Nthis lineup isn't too bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.19,0:07:03.05,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,He may have a big mouth, \Nbut Gilbert is decently strong.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.58,0:07:07.91,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,Greg has a lot of experience, \Nso he coordinates well with others.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.29,0:07:12.05,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,Rhuda doesn't do anything too flashy,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.05,0:07:14.36,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,but as a thief, she's an \Nexpert at locating enemies.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.44,0:07:18.36,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,If she hadn't been here,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.36,0:07:21.06,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,I wouldn't have been able \Nto focus on combat.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.15,0:07:26.05,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Every single detail was calculated.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.05,0:07:28.26,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,As I thought, Master was right.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.29,0:07:32.17,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Master {\i1}is {\i0}a god.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.65,0:07:36.24,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,Damn it! You think I'm playing around?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.66,0:07:38.68,Flashback Internal,Gilbert(M),0,0,0,,Are you guys playing around?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.99,0:07:41.05,Flashback,Gilbert,0,0,0,,You need to have more guts!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.05,0:07:42.21,Flashback,Suman,0,0,0,,Sorry...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.21,0:07:45.12,Flashback,Genkai,0,0,0,,We can barely manage \Nto keep up with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.12,0:07:48.12,Flashback,Gilbert,0,0,0,,That's it! I'm done!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.88,0:07:49.87,Flashback Top,Genkai,0,0,0,,Gilbert!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.58,0:07:51.75,Internal,Gilbert(M),0,0,0,,It's not like they weren't trying.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.87,0:07:51.02,Flashback Top,Suman,0,0,0,,Gilbert...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.75,0:07:54.95,Internal,Gilbert(M),0,0,0,,But the gap between us \Nonly kept getting bigger.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.32,0:07:57.64,Flashback,Gilbert,0,0,0,,I've had enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.64,0:07:59.01,Flashback,Gilbert,0,0,0,,I'm leaving.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.86,0:08:03.09,Internal,Gilbert(M),0,0,0,,Back then, I was so full of anger.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.70,0:08:06.95,Internal,Gilbert(M),0,0,0,,Now I understand \Nthat they were desperate.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.26,0:08:11.01,Internal,Gilbert(M),0,0,0,,I had never even \Nconsidered their feelings.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.30,0:08:18.24,Internal,Gilbert(M),0,0,0,,I never knew...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.68,0:08:22.06,Internal,Gilbert(M),0,0,0,,that fighting side by side with \Na team could feel this good...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.55,0:08:31.14,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,You're not half bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.87,0:08:36.58,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,I'm finally getting warmed up.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.58,0:08:37.95,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,You don't say.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.96,0:08:43.92,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,This place sure opened up.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.17,0:08:46.35,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.35,0:08:47.58,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,There's someone here.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.58,0:08:48.83,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,The rescue targets?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.31,0:08:52.10,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,No, most likely, it's the boss.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.10,0:08:56.31,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Master's missions usually have a big one.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.69,0:09:00.93,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,Shouldn't we run away?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.29,0:09:04.35,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,We managed to get this \Nfar without a scratch.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.35,0:09:05.94,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,We should be able to \Nhandle the boss, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.58,0:09:10.53,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Greg, a big guy like\Nyou shouldn't be so cautious.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.66,0:09:14.30,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Safe missions don't make people grow.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.76,0:09:16.86,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Caution is generally good,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.86,0:09:18.82,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,but sometimes you need \Nto throw it to the wind.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.22,0:09:20.83,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,Well, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.70,0:09:25.05,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,You're not entirely wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.85,0:09:28.37,Internal,Greg,0,0,0,,Once a hunter reaches level 4,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.37,0:09:32.55,Internal,Greg,0,0,0,,they can make a fine living just by \Ncompleting treasure vaults below their level.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.36,0:09:37.37,Internal,Greg,0,0,0,,Whenever I thought that I couldn't win, \NI stopped engaging the enemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.52,0:09:44.16,Internal,Greg,0,0,0,,This was in no doubt influenced by \Nseeing many of my friends die.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.09,0:09:49.05,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Despite being in the \Nhunter biz for so long,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.05,0:09:54.22,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,you approached First Steps \Nbecause you wanted to change that.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.60,0:09:55.81,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,That's...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.81,0:09:59.24,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,That is the reason Master \Nplaced you into this party.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.24,0:10:00.07,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.07,0:10:04.87,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Otherwise, why would he choose \Nsomeone he barely knew?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.20,0:10:06.17,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.17,0:10:09.75,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Master wanted to save {\i1}all {\i0}of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.60,0:10:11.37,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,That is to say,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.77,0:10:15.59,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Master is a god.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.13,0:10:22.23,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Did you really think Master \Nput this group together randomly?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.23,0:10:25.14,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,He's not the kind to throw spaghetti\Nat the wall to see what sticks.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.48,0:10:28.07,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,All of this has been according\Nto his inscrutable plan
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.07,0:10:30.29,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,and elaborate calculations.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.83,0:10:32.89,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Obviously, he's a god.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.29,0:10:36.87,Default,Rhuda,0,0,0,,Uh, so why did he pick {\i1}me{\i0}?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.57,0:10:47.37,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Maybe 'cause you've got big boobs?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.34,0:10:50.27,Default,Rhuda,0,0,0,,Hey, wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.27,0:10:51.51,Default,Rhuda,0,0,0,,What is {\i1}that{\i0} supposed to mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.51,0:10:53.07,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Stop playing around.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.07,0:10:54.77,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Let's go beat up that boss already.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.77,0:10:55.93,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,Y-Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.93,0:10:56.41,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.01,0:10:59.10,Default,Rhuda,0,0,0,,Jeez.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.10,0:11:00.49,Default,Rhuda,0,0,0,,Wait up!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.82,0:11:04.24,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,I can't see Tino anywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.24,0:11:06.68,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,Does that mean that I'm too late?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.91,0:11:09.67,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,Either way, this relic \Ngoes too damn fast!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.67,0:11:14.69,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,What the hell was the creator thinking, \Nmaking this thing with no brakes?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.69,0:11:16.31,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,Too fast! Too scary!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.31,0:11:17.56,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,I'm gonna die!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.94,0:11:30.37,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,So this is... the boss...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.67,0:11:32.88,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,He's way too damn big!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.00,0:11:41.16,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,He's strong.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.16,0:11:42.26,Internal,Gilbert(M),0,0,0,,Now what?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.26,0:11:43.76,Internal,Greg(M),0,0,0,,Do we retreat?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.51,0:11:47.90,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,This boss isn't wearing a helmet...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.90,0:11:50.65,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,which means that \Nmust be its weak point.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.65,0:11:54.03,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,This is one of Master's Thousand Trials.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.03,0:11:55.87,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,I {\i0}will{\i1} overcome this!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.87,0:11:57.28,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Block one of his blows.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.28,0:11:58.41,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,I'll take it from there.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.41,0:11:59.63,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,Got it!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.77,0:12:03.74,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,All right. Shall we?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.74,0:12:04.39,Default,Rhuda,0,0,0,,Let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.68,0:12:11.04,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,So heavy!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.97,0:12:25.24,Internal,Rhuda(M),0,0,0,,I can't see a hint of fear on that girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.64,0:12:26.65,Internal,Rhuda(M),0,0,0,,She's amazing.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.34,0:12:31.92,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,It broke!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.19,0:12:34.18,Default,Rhuda,0,0,0,,Greg!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.25,0:12:51.32,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,She got him!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.32,0:12:52.52,Default,Rhuda,0,0,0,,She did?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.52,0:12:53.70,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,She did it...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.60,0:12:58.65,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,We win.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.15,0:13:02.43,Default,Rhuda,0,0,0,,Tino, is your leg all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.43,0:13:03.65,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,It's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.65,0:13:05.00,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,I've got a potion.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.34,0:13:09.45,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,Damn.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.45,0:13:12.52,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,Of all the times for my sword to break... \NThis just isn't my day.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.52,0:13:15.07,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,At least you're alive, old man.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.20,0:13:17.59,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,You're damn right.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.10,0:13:20.37,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,Thanks, Rhuda.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.37,0:13:21.27,Default,Rhuda,0,0,0,,Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.27,0:13:24.11,Default,Rhuda,0,0,0,,I'm just glad I managed \Nto get to you in time.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.41,0:13:27.38,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,Now all that's left is the rescue.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.66,0:13:29.48,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.88,0:13:33.41,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,You can have this.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.41,0:13:35.12,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,It's better than nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.12,0:13:36.11,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,R-Right...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.84,0:13:38.27,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.35,0:13:50.08,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,What the hell?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.61,0:13:53.68,Default,Rhuda,0,0,0,,You mean there's more than one boss?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.68,0:13:55.21,Default,Rhuda,0,0,0,,But it's {\i1}a boss{\i0}!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.75,0:13:58.46,Default,Rhuda,0,0,0,,This can't be happening!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.76,0:14:00.08,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,Master...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.43,0:14:03.30,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,This second helping... \Nreally is too much.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.65,0:14:05.26,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,Wh-What do we do?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.26,0:14:06.50,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.50,0:14:07.76,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,We have no choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.75,0:14:09.95,Default,Rhuda,0,0,0,,Tino!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.95,0:14:12.28,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,We'll run into the \Nnearest passage on the right.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.28,0:14:14.37,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,A passage that narrow will \Nhave a low ceiling, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.37,0:14:16.71,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,They won't be able to swing\Ntheir swords and clubs in there.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.80,0:14:20.29,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,He blocked it?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.13,0:14:24.11,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,We'll be the bait.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.11,0:14:25.15,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,There's no other option.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.15,0:14:26.33,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,Tino, Rhuda.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.33,0:14:28.56,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,The two of you should be nimble \Nenough to break through.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.56,0:14:30.36,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,Do whatever you can to escape!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.36,0:14:31.46,Default,Rhuda,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.46,0:14:33.48,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,It's better than all of us dying.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.56,0:14:36.83,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,Don't dwell on it too much.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.83,0:14:38.44,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,It happens all the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.44,0:14:40.83,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,It's our turn now, is all.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.41,0:14:46.30,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,Is this really the only \Nthing we can do, Master?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.45,0:14:51.58,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,Master!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.16,0:14:55.13,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,I already told you, \Nwe're not sacrificing anyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.13,0:14:55.91,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,Tino...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.00,0:14:59.20,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,We have to go for their eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.59,0:15:00.81,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,I'll do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.81,0:15:02.27,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Please back me up.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.71,0:15:10.46,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,Take this!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.33,0:15:26.77,Flashback,Tino,0,0,0,,I did it!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.78,0:15:30.02,Flashback,Tino,0,0,0,,Master, I did it!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.18,0:15:32.28,Flashback,Krai,0,0,0,,You did well.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.28,0:15:34.93,Flashback,Tino,0,0,0,,All because of your tutelage.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.30,0:15:37.46,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Master...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.06,0:15:52.12,Default,Rhuda,0,0,0,,Now!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.12,0:15:53.05,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.93,0:15:56.07,Internal,Gilbert(M),0,0,0,,If we can get him now...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.45,0:15:57.31,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Don't!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.52,0:16:05.90,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Gilbert!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.84,0:16:10.03,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.31,0:16:12.77,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,No. My directions\N weren't good enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.08,0:16:14.82,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,You did nothing wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.63,0:16:22.03,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,I guess this is it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.19,0:16:31.79,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,Ow, ow, ow...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.21,0:16:34.26,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,M-Master?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.71,0:16:37.67,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,I spy a Tino!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.46,0:16:39.86,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Master!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.02,0:16:45.18,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,Are they... scared?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.58,0:16:46.41,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.81,0:16:52.44,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,What is this huge thing?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.82,0:17:13.58,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,Too bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.93,0:17:18.33,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,I've got 17 lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.91,0:17:33.22,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,So {\i1}this{\i0} is a level 8?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.22,0:17:34.87,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,Wh-Whoa...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.87,0:17:36.48,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Master!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.92,0:17:39.31,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,I didn't really mean to \Nshow off like that...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.31,0:17:40.57,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,But what is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.57,0:17:42.50,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,What are all these terrifying things?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.80,0:17:45.72,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,This is a level 3 \Ntreasure vault, right?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.00,0:17:53.25,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,What the—?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.09,0:17:57.51,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,He ate all those attacks, and still...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.51,0:18:01.36,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,I mean, yeah. Shooting Rings \Nare not that powerful.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.36,0:18:02.52,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,They're just flashy.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.73,0:18:06.02,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,So, once again.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.43,0:18:08.28,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,Why bows and guns?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.28,0:18:09.53,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,That doesn't make any sense!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.53,0:18:14.02,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,Sure am glad I brought 17 Safety Rings.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.46,0:18:17.18,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,I don't even care about\Nthe rescue mission anymore!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.18,0:18:19.53,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,I just wanna go home!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.73,0:18:24.23,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,I've got no choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.23,0:18:25.54,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,Now that it's come to this,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.81,0:18:26.70,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,I'll take this, and...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.74,0:18:54.46,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,Tino, run!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.46,0:18:55.75,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Y-Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.38,0:18:57.28,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,You, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.28,0:18:58.33,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.29,0:19:04.45,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,Hey, at this pace,\Nthey'll catch us in no time!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.45,0:19:07.20,Default,Rhuda,0,0,0,,Tino is hurt, you idiot!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.20,0:19:10.53,Default,Rhuda,0,0,0,,Krai's deliberately setting a slower pace \Nas the rearguard with that in mind!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.53,0:19:11.72,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,M-My bad!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.97,0:19:12.83,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.83,0:19:14.71,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,I'm running at full tilt here!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.28,0:19:22.98,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,Master, that casual kindness reminds \Nme of the first time we met...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.92,0:19:27.73,Flashback,Zuro,0,0,0,,Nobody's coming to save you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.73,0:19:29.45,Flashback,Zuro,0,0,0,,You're on your own.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.45,0:19:30.96,Flashback,Ratma,0,0,0,,This'll be over quick.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.96,0:19:32.97,Flashback,Ratma,0,0,0,,She'll fetch a good price.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.61,0:19:39.11,Flashback,Tino,0,0,0,,Help...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.02,0:19:42.36,Flashback,Zuro,0,0,0,,What the hell?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.36,0:19:44.83,Flashback,Lucia,0,0,0,,You two are in the way.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.83,0:19:45.68,Flashback,Ansem,0,0,0,,Yup.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.68,0:19:47.99,Flashback,Stiri,0,0,0,,It's because you're standing there.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.99,0:19:48.89,Flashback,Luke,0,0,0,,Take that!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.21,0:19:51.36,Flashback,Liz,0,0,0,,Die!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.63,0:19:55.11,Flashback,Ratma,0,0,0,,Let's split!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.56,0:19:57.97,Flashback,Zuro,0,0,0,,Grieving Souls, eh?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.97,0:19:59.17,Flashback,Zuro,0,0,0,,I won't forget this!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.17,0:20:00.84,Flashback,Luke,0,0,0,,Man, they ran away!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.84,0:20:01.90,Flashback,Krai,0,0,0,,That's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.90,0:20:02.67,Flashback,Ansem,0,0,0,,Yup.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.67,0:20:05.79,Flashback,Tino,0,0,0,,Excuse me, but may I know your name?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.76,0:20:09.66,Flashback,Krai,0,0,0,,We're not that special.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.24,0:20:13.64,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,I've wanted to join the Grievers ever since.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.70,0:20:17.68,Internal,Tino(M),0,0,0,,And Master is... a god!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.62,0:20:20.20,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,We made it out...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.20,0:20:21.52,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,That was close.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.52,0:20:23.32,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,You saved us.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.32,0:20:23.98,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.98,0:20:24.90,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,Oh. Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.37,0:20:27.16,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,M-Master.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.97,0:20:31.03,Default,Rhuda,0,0,0,,Krai, Tino did so well!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.03,0:20:34.35,Default,Rhuda,0,0,0,,If it wasn't for her, I bet \Nwe'd all be dead by now.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.35,0:20:35.66,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,Yeah, I can imagine.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.08,0:20:38.46,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.89,0:20:42.10,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,How nice would it be if that \Nword could solve anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.10,0:20:43.30,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,I-It's okay...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.68,0:20:47.75,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,I can tell you did well \Njust by looking at you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.30,0:20:49.64,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Master!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.25,0:20:55.16,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,She really got beaten up...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.46,0:20:59.32,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,Huh? What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.04,0:21:01.77,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,Oh, I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.77,0:21:03.47,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Uhh, it hurts.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.47,0:21:04.95,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,It hurts.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.95,0:21:05.86,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,Hold on.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.58,0:21:14.88,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Thank you so much, Master!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.88,0:21:17.13,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,It doesn't hurt anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.13,0:21:18.34,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,Yup, yup.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.69,0:21:21.35,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,I guess he uses a relic for healing.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.61,0:21:24.84,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,I need a relic for every single thing \NI do. Got a problem with that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.13,0:21:28.45,Default,Greg,0,0,0,,Krai, did you defeat those bosses?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.45,0:21:29.73,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,I did not.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.73,0:21:32.80,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,In the moment, \Nthat was the best option.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.80,0:21:35.40,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,But that's not what we need to \Nbe thinking about right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.40,0:21:36.77,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,Anyway, let's walk.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.77,0:21:38.29,Default,Gilbert,0,0,0,,S-Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.35,0:21:45.87,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,So now...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.23,0:21:48.62,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,The real issue is... Where even are we,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.62,0:21:51.26,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,and where is the exit?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.87,0:21:56.88,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,Seriously, what do I do?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.88,0:21:58.86,Internal,Krai(M),0,0,0,,I'm gonna puke.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.47,0:22:01.80,Internal,Narrator,0,0,0,,Our Krai Andrey forges ahead
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.80,0:22:04.51,Internal,Narrator,0,0,0,,with the expectations of the other \Nfour resting on his shoulders.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:04.51,0:22:07.13,Internal,Narrator,0,0,0,,But isn't he forgetting about the \Npeople who need to be rescued?!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.13,0:22:11.35,Internal,Narrator,0,0,0,,Can our Krai Andrey \Nactually save them?!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.35,0:22:14.42,Internal,Narrator,0,0,0,,Please tune in again next time!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.84,0:23:31.15,Top,Tino,0,0,0,,Hey, yo! Stupid wolves wearing skulls!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.63,0:23:44.65,EpTitle,txt,0,0,0,,{\fs15\pos(482.429,355)}By: Tino Shade & Wall Spaghetti Party
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.15,0:23:32.64,Top,Greg,0,0,0,,A bunch of them came out and gave us grief.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.64,0:23:34.13,Top,Gilbert,0,0,0,,The long, winding White Wolf's Labyrinth.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.13,0:23:35.75,Top,Rhuda,0,0,0,,We have no plan but we forge ahead!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.75,0:23:37.28,Top,Greg,0,0,0,,Again, more of those skull jerks!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.28,0:23:38.96,Top,Gilbert,0,0,0,,This is serious trouble!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.96,0:23:41.03,Top,Tino,0,0,0,,Huh? What? That can't be!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:41.03,0:23:42.03,Top,Rhuda,0,0,0,,What happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.03,0:23:43.94,Top,Tino,0,0,0,,Next time, on {\i1}Let This Grieving Soul{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.94,0:23:44.98,Top,All,0,0,0,,...{\i1}Retire{\i0}!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.65,0:23:49.94,EpTitle,Title,0,0,0,,{\c&H00BAFF&\pos(320.52,100.623)}Episode 04
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.65,0:23:49.94,EpTitle,Title,0,0,0,,{\fs30\bord3\pos(322.143,238.714)\c&HD1D1D1&}The Mysterious Mask Wants to Fight
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.98,0:23:47.24,Default,Tino,0,0,0,,Please forgive me! Please forgive me! I'm sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.24,0:23:49.28,Default,Krai,0,0,0,,"The Mysterious Mask Wants to Fight."
